  "description": "Envelope vectors (RFC-0003 'Envelope'), written by `cargo xtask gen-vectors`. A reader expects schema `schema` whose writers emit version `version`, so it accepts `version` and `version - 1` but never 0. It reads under `limits`, or under the RFC-0003 defaults a case names, which every implementation takes from its own constants. It checks `hex` in the order RFC-0003 fixes, then decodes the payload as `type`, which must fill it. It returns `payload`, or fails with `code` at `offset`, counted from the start of the envelope. A rejection has one fault, except the cases that pin which of two faults is reported.",
